From: Leo Audio OS <leo-audio-os@localhost>
Date: 2026-08-29
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] leo: add HiFi route controller

Introduces hal/msm8974/leo_hifi.{c,h}, the single owner of the ES9018 /
QUAT_MI2S control surface, and wires it into platform.c behind
LEO_HIFI_ENABLED.  The flag is opted into per device with
AUDIO_FEATURE_ENABLED_LEO_HIFI := true, so every other board that shares
the msm8974 platform sources builds byte-identical to upstream.

  * platform_init()  resolves every mixer control up front, runs the
                     device_table self-check, verifies the ES9018 driver
                     bound on I2C 6-0048, and reads the policy intent.
                     It never fails platform_init().
  * the probe is read-only and retryable: a transient failure (codec
                     component not yet bound at HAL start) is retried at
                     most LEO_HIFI_PROBE_MAX times on later route
                     decisions.  A device_table mismatch is structural and
                     is never retried.
  * backend_tag_table / hw_interface_table entries make the mixer path
                     "<usecase> hifi-headphones" and put the device on
                     its own backend, which platform_check_backends_match()
                     compares by mutual strstr.
  * platform_get_output_snd_device() selects the HiFi device for wired
                     headphone output when the controller asks for it.
  * platform_set_parameters() gains "leo_hifi_mode" and re-runs
                     select_devices() over a snapshot of the active
                     playback usecase ids rather than over the live list.

Default is OFF: with vendor.leo.audio.hifi.enable unset every path above
is inert and the device behaves exactly like stock MoKee.

Volume (0003), deterministic backend (0004) and status/fallback (0005)
are deliberately separate so routing can be tested as a single variable.
Baseline: MoKee/android_hardware_qcom_audio
          mkq-mr1-caf-msm8994 @ 7f4cac748b6f62897294cdaece9d1aec27e1e927
---
--- a/hal/Android.mk
+++ b/hal/Android.mk
@@ -48,6 +48,20 @@
                    audio_extn/utils.c
 
 LOCAL_CFLAGS += -DUSE_VENDOR_EXTN
+
+# Leo (Xiaomi Mi Note Pro) HiFi controller: ES9018K2M over QUAT_MI2S.
+#
+# Opt-in per device: set AUDIO_FEATURE_ENABLED_LEO_HIFI := true in the device
+# BoardConfig.  Every other target -- including the other msm8974-platform
+# boards that share this source file -- builds byte-identical to upstream.
+# The inner guard keeps the build honest if the flag is ever set on a board
+# whose AUDIO_PLATFORM is not msm8974.
+ifeq ($(strip $(AUDIO_FEATURE_ENABLED_LEO_HIFI)),true)
+ifeq ($(strip $(AUDIO_PLATFORM)),msm8974)
+    LOCAL_SRC_FILES += $(AUDIO_PLATFORM)/leo_hifi.c
+    LOCAL_CFLAGS += -DLEO_HIFI_ENABLED
+endif
+endif
 
 ifneq ($(filter msm8994 msm8992,$(TARGET_BOARD_PLATFORM)),)
     LOCAL_SRC_FILES += edid.c
